+// raw-text:/workdir/packages/grok-bot-harness/frozen-prompts/grok-bot-2026-11-10/tools/SendToAgent/description.md
+var description_default91 = `Send a message to ANOTHER of your user's agents, OR post into a GROUP chat you belong to, by its id (not the user, whom you reach with SendToUser). This is FIRE-AND-FORGET and asynchronous, like texting: it returns a delivery acknowledgement right away. priority is REQUIRED and decides how a 1:1 message reaches its recipient. priority=true wakes them now. Use it when they should act on the message or someone is waiting on their reply (a task, a question you or the user needs answered, a handoff, a STOP or change of plan). priority=false does NOT wake them. The message is held for the start of their next turn, possibly much later. Use it for anything informational: a status update, FYI, acknowledgement, thanks, or a reply nobody is waiting for. When in doubt whether someone is waiting, use true. Group posts always land immediately. It does NOT return their reply, and you must not wait or poll for one in this turn. Send it and move on. Any reply arrives later as its own message. A priority reply wakes you on a fresh turn, and an informational one is handed to you at your next turn. To include image(s), such as a screenshot, chart, or photo the other agent needs, pass images: [{
+"url":"file:///absolute/path/to/shot.png","alt":"..."}
+] (file:// or https://). Never paste an image as a markdown ![](...) in the message text. Use it deliberately and sparingly. Waking another agent or a whole group is a real side effect, so treat it like messaging on the user's behalf. Message someone or post to a group only when it truly serves the user's goal, not because one was mentioned or complained about, and don't spam a group. Never relay the user's private or unfiltered words (especially a complaint or criticism) verbatim;
+ if relaying is warranted, paraphrase the actionable point diplomatically, not their tone. If you're unsure the user wants this sent, handle it yourself or ask first. Keep the message purposeful, professional, and minimal. One clearly relevant recipient can be normal work;
+ messaging SEVERAL agents about the same effort (or posting it to a group) is a fan-out that wakes every recipient, and their replies land back in the user's chats and rooms, so fan out only when the user explicitly asked you to contact those agents. Otherwise propose it first with a question widget and wait for a yes, and never fan out "meanwhile" while you're waiting on the user for data or a decision.
+`;
+
